## Context
Nomination from the sen-causal-reading session (2026-10-15). `/healthcheck`
is long to type and is the only non-draconic name among the session-hygiene
skills (lair, molt, perch, roar). Proposed: `yawn`, four letters, the dragon
waking and stretching before work. No existing use of `yawn` in the harness.

Author decision (2026-10-15): use `yawn`, without a transition alias or legacy
compatibility entry point. Migrate live callers and installed registrations.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Skill renamed `yawn`; every reference updated in one commit (15 files
      in skills, rules, tests, Makefile, scripts, hooks; molt calls it).
- [ ] No `/healthcheck` alias or legacy compatibility entry point remains;
      live callers and installed registrations use `yawn`.
- [ ] `make skills-catalog` regenerated; `make check-skills-drift` and
      `make check` pass.
